WEBVTT

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:05.940
The Power of Order will awaken and confront the Black Power

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.900
in order to negate the destiny that is inherent to this world.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:16.240
Is that not proof that she, the Master Unit, desires the future?

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:20.450
But that's not the future we desire.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.660
What we desire is tranquility.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.790
We will select and tune a better future within this Continuum Shift,

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:33.380
and construct a perfect world that will stand firm.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:37.220
By the way, about Yuuki Terumi.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:40.720
Is he not already beyond your control?

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:45.310
With regards to the Yuuki Terumi events, they are all within expected parameters.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:49.820
As for the interference due to the use of the Anti-Surveyor Weapon Izayoi,

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:52.690
it will be dealt with as part of the Continuum Shift.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:58.410
Isn't it <i>you we should be worrying about, Rachel Alucard?</i>

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:03.620
Are you forgetting your place as an observer and intend to interfere once again?

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:05.000
I'm hurt.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:08.210
I am the successor of the Tsukuyomi Unit.

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:11.340
The purpose of my existence is to protect the Master Unit.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.340
Besides, the world that you desire...

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.510
...seems so dull.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:56.150
Rebel 10: The God-Killer's Cocoon

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:00.320
Too slow.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.410
I finally understand.

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:07.620
No, I have conviction now.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:08.830
Huh?

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:10.960
All the evil trends...

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:13.710
The one at the center of them all is you, Brother!

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:15.540
What are you on about, you nut—

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:24.890
You are none other than the source of the evil leading the world to its ruin.

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:28.100
But rest easy, Brother.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:31.560
I won't let anyone kill you.

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:34.060
After all,

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:35.560
that's <i>my</i> job!

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:37.820
Jin!

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.000
<i>This guy!</i>

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:56.090
What's wrong, Brother?!

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:59.380
That's not even close to what you're really capable of, or is it?!

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:01.720
You spoiled little kid!

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:03.760
Shadowless, echoless...

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:06.800
Kokuujin.

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:09.220
Wha—

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:10.680
Yukikaze!

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.690
Weak! You're so weak, Brother!

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:22.650
How can this fight be enjoyable now?!

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:25.110
Well I sure as hell ain't enjoying it!

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.250
Mr. Tager...

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.920
So he's the man from Sector Seven you were talking about?

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:42.300
Second Lieutenant Makoto Nanaya, your hard work is much appreciated.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:46.180
You've done a splendid job of escorting Second Lieutenant Noel Vermillion here.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:48.800
That will do for now. Dismissed.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:49.390
What?

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:52.350
I do not recall receiving such an order.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.850
Oh, is that so?

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:58.900
I thought you were being a zealous subordinate and anticipating her superior's demands.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:00.610
Indeed.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:06.660
This Continuum Shift was prepared just for Noel Vermillion.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:08.280
Huh? For me?

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:09.780
Precisely!

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:14.410
Goodness! Setting up the stage was such a hassle!

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:16.250
So, you see...

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:20.290
If the supporting cast could make a swift exit, that'd be just peachy.

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:22.710
You should take a cue from First Lieutenant Tsubaki Yayoi.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:23.510
What?!

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:24.670
What did you do to Tsubaki?!

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:27.630
Oh, don't look at me like that.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:30.220
Do I have to remind you that I'm your superior officer?

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:33.680
You? My superior officer? Don't make me laugh!

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:35.520
Oh, I see how it is.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:41.110
Just a moment ago, you were addressing the Red Devil as "Mr. Tager".

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:46.490
Could it be that <i>someone</i> is all buddy-buddy with Sector Seven?!

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:48.490
How deplorable!

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:52.030
I'm ashamed to learn that one of my very own subordinates has turned rebel!

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:54.450
Noel, let's split up and run.

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:55.540
Huh? But...

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:58.250
Trust me. Noel, you go that way.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.630
Going somewhere?

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:01.590
Wha—

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:05.420
Makoto!

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:09.800
Bolverk!

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:23.650
Whoopsie-daisy!

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:28.150
Makoto, are you okay?

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.570
Leave this to me.

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:32.320
Noel, you hurry and—

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:33.330
I can't do that, Makoto!

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:36.790
I won't run away and leave a friend behind ever again!

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.540
Let's go get Tsubaki together!

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:41.500
Yeah, you're right.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.670
We've got Tsubaki to worry about.

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:44.750
Yeah!

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:46.800
That's why we're in this together!

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.300
Guess we'll do it!

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:56.140
Good grief... Violence is such an uncultured thing to resort to.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:00.810
I'm not quite done self-repairing...

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:02.690
Don't move if you're not ready yet, Tager.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:05.320
Kokonoe, things are looking grim here.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:06.570
Yeah, tell me about it.

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:10.530
That's why I'm directing all your remaining energy to restoring the transfer system.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.660
What?! Hey, hold on! What about Makoto Nanaya?!

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:15.490
Right now, transferring Lambda comes first.

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:16.240
But...

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:19.370
Sorry, but I have no intention of debating this with you.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:20.500
Hey, Kokonoe—

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:24.750
Sorry.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.180
Yikes!

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:37.390
Whoops, that was close.

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:41.890
Take that!

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:43.230
Wha—

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:46.900
Shit.

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:55.160
What?! What's that?

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:56.950
Ouroboros!

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:08.880
What the hell do you think you're doing, you stinking Beastkin?

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:31.030
Don't you worry. I'll be <i>real</i> nice to you later.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:34.400
Why don't you take a nap 'til then?

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.040
Now, then.

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:43.000
You sure are a cocky one.

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:48.710
Don't think you'll get a painless death, Beastkin.

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:55.880
Shit!

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:59.180
How does Terumi keep appearing at the worst possible time?

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:04.600
I guess I'd better assume that they know what we'll do.

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:09.230
In that case, I just have to aim for a time when his attention is focused elsewhere.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:14.070
I need something that'll make him look the other way...

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:17.780
It still has to be Ragna the Bloodedge.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.830
C'mon. What's the matter?

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:27.040
You gonna die?

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:28.580
You gonna wind up dead?

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:33.760
Makoto...

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:37.590
Eh?

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:39.850
So, the sleeping beauty awakens.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:44.680
Makoto!

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:46.270
Stay right there!

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:50.730
Think about what might happen to you disgusting Beastkin friend here.

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:54.400
Oh my, that's quite a fall.

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:56.450
Doesn't look like you'd be able to catch her, either.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:58.240
Let her go!

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:02.780
Let her go? Who do you think you're talking to,

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:04.830
Doll?!

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:09.040
Makoto!

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:14.000
Well color me surprised! Even the gross Beastkin's blood is red!

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:16.920
Stop that!

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:18.720
Like I said,

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:21.930
you're nothing but a damn doll, stop ordering me around!

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:29.230
Enough already! Makoto is going to die!

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:31.940
Are you deaf?!

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:36.110
I don't take orders from <i>dolls</i>!

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:40.910
I'm sorry. Please.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:43.910
I'm begging you. Stop this already.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:48.870
Whose fault do you think it is that this is happening to the Beastkin?

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:50.120
Do you even know?

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:52.160
Tell me.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:54.840
Don't... ask...

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:56.420
Can it, you!

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:01.930
Dead? She dead?

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:09.690
Nice job, Beastkin! Still clingin' on to life!

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:13.440
I implore you! Just stop...

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:14.980
Shut the hell up.

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:17.150
You seriously don't get it?

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:20.780
You still don't realize whose fault it is that she's suffering?

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:22.530
That's...

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:26.280
It's <i>your</i> fault, Noel Vermillion!

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:29.910
It's because you exist in this world!

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:31.710
Because of me?

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:32.710
That's right.

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:40.510
The distortion named Noel Vermillion disrupts the lives of this Beastkin—no, the entire world!

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:43.180
<i>You</i>, who by all rights should not exist!

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:45.760
Shouldn't... exist?

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:49.600
Yeah, you're a being who shouldn't exist.

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:54.230
Because you appeared, Tsubaki Yayoi lost her place!

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:57.270
All because of the distortion that is you!

00:11:58.020 --> 00:12:00.150
Man, how messed up.

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:05.530
Because of you, her worthless existence just got even worse!

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:08.120
Stop saying that stuff about Tsubaki!

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:12.330
I call a spade a spade.

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:15.500
But I already told you, remember?

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:18.380
Even that worthless girl had her moment of happiness.

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:21.590
But <i>you</i> had to butt in and take it away!

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:22.470
I did not—

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:25.430
You should be able to see it.

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:35.690
This is the truth known as despair!

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:38.770
No!

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:41.490
You saw it, right? You <i>saw</i> it!

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:43.360
You should've been able to perceive it!

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:45.950
The world where you don't exist.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:48.070
<i>That</i> is the truth!

00:12:48.070 --> 00:12:50.330
It's a lie... It's a lie...

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:52.080
It can't be...

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:57.750
The Azure Successor, the Calamity Trigger.

00:12:57.750 --> 00:13:03.380
That's you. It's your existence that's throwing this world out of whack!

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.220
Now...

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:17.850
This might not be a bad time to wrap up the chitchat.

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:19.980
Heyo, you still kickin' up there?

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:27.610
You sure are a stubborn one.

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:32.870
Makoto...

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:35.410
Makoto!

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:46.970
From this height, I doubt even she'd survive the fall.

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:52.560
You won't get away with this...

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:56.520
I'll never let you get away with it!

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:58.690
I like that look on your face!

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:01.980
Yes! Feel more hatred! More!

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:04.110
Come on!

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:05.780
You're not getting away with it...

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:07.450
I'll make <i>sure</i> you don't!

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:10.530
That's it! Pull the trigger!

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:12.990
Pull the Calamity Trigger!

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:15.950
I will...

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:18.460
I will annihilate you!

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:22.170
Yes, good! Quickly, pull the trigger!

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:25.380
Pull it, you damn doll!

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:30.260
I hate you...

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:32.300
I hate you so much.

00:14:33.050 --> 00:14:34.140
I hate you!

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:37.600
I hate you. I hate you. I hate you. I hate you. I hate you!

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:47.690
She finally disengaged her limiter!

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:50.200
Hate!

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:54.330
Hate me! Hate the world! Hate yourself!

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:56.160
Use your Eye to <i>see</i>!

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:58.710
See the world's despair!

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:03.130
I am... a doll.

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:06.090
Then I don't need it.

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:10.050
I don't need it.

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:11.340
That's right.

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:15.180
The world rejects you. Mankind reject you.

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:16.890
They don't want a doll in their world!

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:19.850
Now what will you do, Twelfth Prime Field?!

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:25.270
Now! Unleash your hatred! Unleash your madness!

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:26.780
Come!

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:29.280
Come with me into the darkness!

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:32.240
I don't need... this world...

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:59.520
With this, I have control of everything!

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:12.360
What is it?

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:18.660
Sorry, but we'll have to wait to settle things!

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:19.290
Damn!

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:24.290
You.

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:25.790
Don't go, Jin!

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:28.750
Step aside, or I'll cut you down.

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:32.050
You must head for the Cauldron underground.

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:34.220
And then wait there.

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:35.550
To the Cauldron?

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:36.800
That's right!

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:38.100
You think I'll simply obey you?

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:42.060
If you truly wish to fight Ragna...

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.400
What's there?

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:47.190
Go and you'll see.

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:02.660
You are the ones who must change the world.

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:17.800
So, you came.

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:20.220
That was faster than I'd expected.

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:23.730
Terumi!

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:25.980
Where's Noel?!

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:27.730
Noel?

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:29.730
Ah, you mean Noel Vermillion.

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:31.690
Take a look over there.

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:33.820
This sensation...

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:35.280
Don't tell me...

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:39.870
Oh, you're awfully quick on the uptake, Rags.

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:41.740
Is that a Cauldron?

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:42.990
Bingo!

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:44.290
Did you take Noel to...

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:47.500
What else would I do to her?

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:50.880
Terumi!

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:57.260
Bastard! Stop the smelting right now!

00:17:57.260 --> 00:17:59.720
You think that's going to make me stop?

00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:01.930
Damn it!

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:05.640
Noel, hang in there! I'm coming for you!

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:09.020
Oh, gosh. Is that the Azure Grimoire?

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:10.980
How frightening!

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:13.940
Restriction 666 released.

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:18.740
Dimensional Interference Field deployed!

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:23.030
Azure Grimoire, activate!

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:27.000
What?!

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:28.330
How?

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:30.330
But you're...

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:40.640
The great hero, tied up in chains and locked in a cage.

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:45.720
This place is certainly lacking in elegance.

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:47.310
Enough with the quips.

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:51.560
Terumi has taken Noel.

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:57.360
And so, Mr. Hero, fulfill your role.

00:18:57.360 --> 00:19:02.370
That would be eliminating the Azure Successor.

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:05.370
I'm fine with that.

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:07.540
You mean to repeat the cycle again?

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:08.960
I suppose.

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:14.790
Losing the Master Unit, however, is not an option.

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:18.760
In that case, I accept my duty.

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:21.840
Though it deeply vexes me to do your bidding.

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:23.090
You wound me.

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:25.970
I'm more amiable than Kokonoe, at least.

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:28.810
So, what will you do?

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:32.520
This restraint circle is more than even you can handle.

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:34.650
Oh, really?

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:45.740
A multi-layer punitive restraint circle.

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:48.660
It's an interesting spell, but it has a lot of room for improvement.

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:50.290
You'll find no thanks from me.

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:52.040
Quit it. You're creeping me out.

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:53.210
Let us depart.

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.220
Princess, are you all right?

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:07.810
It's nothing.

00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:12.560
Kokonoe, that barrier you put up was greater than I had imagined.

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:15.230
What?!

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:22.990
This is nothing...

00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:27.580
Thy struggles art futile. 'Tis magic.

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:28.950
Magic?

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:32.620
Are you...

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:36.830
Thou hast gone a little too far with thy games.

00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:38.090
I'm not nearly as bad as you,

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:39.800
Imperator!

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:43.170
An observer should behave as befits an observer

00:20:43.170 --> 00:20:46.680
and appreciate the spectacle from their seat in the audience.

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:52.060
I shall bring down the curtain on this performance.

00:22:22.690 --> 00:22:25.280
How? How could you?!

00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:27.860
"How?", he asks?

00:22:27.860 --> 00:22:30.740
Good question, Rags, m'boy.

00:22:30.950 --> 00:22:32.910
How are you feeling right now, anyway?

00:22:33.700 --> 00:22:35.830
You must not fight Yuuki Terumi.

00:22:35.830 --> 00:22:38.330
There is no winning against him.

00:22:38.920 --> 00:22:39.710
Impossible...

00:22:39.710 --> 00:22:42.920
I like that glint of despair in your eyes. Very nice.

00:22:43.670 --> 00:22:45.250
I haven't seen it for years.

00:22:47.010 --> 00:22:50.260
A word of advice for you:

00:22:51.220 --> 00:22:53.430
the one who created the Azure Grimoire...

00:22:54.350 --> 00:22:55.890
...is me.

00:23:01.350 --> 00:23:04.860
Hazama, I wish to see thee create the Azure Grimoire.

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:05.650
Right now?!

00:23:05.650 --> 00:23:08.190
Episode 11,
"The Murakumo Awakens".

00:23:08.190 --> 00:23:08.990
Done?

00:23:08.990 --> 00:23:10.660
Even I can't do it in that time!
